module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_branch_property_falsified_by_a_derived_push

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_branch_property_falsified_by_a_derived_push: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_branch_property_falsified_by_a_derived_push" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a branch property falsified by a derived push** (an author asserts a property about their OWN branch -- most often \"this change touches only the authority and never its generated projection\" -- and an automated actor then DERIVES the projection onto that same branch after CI. The asserted property was true of the commit the author wrote and false of the branch a reader inspects. This is single-party: no competing author exists and none was omitted. ",

    "INVALID STATE: a published claim about a ref's contents that the ref's own automation can falsify after publication, with nothing that re-checks or withdraws the claim. ",

    "WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW: the claim is TRUE when written and true at review time if review reads the author's commit. The falsifying commit is authored by CI, is independently correct, and arrives after the human attention has moved on. Nothing notifies, because deriving a projection produces no conflict. ",

    "SPECIMEN (PR #10417). The scheme was authority-only editing: touch gunbc.recurring_failure_mode and never docs/design-failure-modes.md. Heal generated the projection onto the branch anyway -- d695b3ab63e is a heal commit adding docs/design-failure-modes.md on top of the author's authority-only commit. The collision property is a fact about the branch AFTER CI, never about the commit the author wrote. Confirmed recurrent rather than incidental, and the OBVIOUS INSTRUMENT FOR THAT IS CONTAMINATED IN THE DIRECTION OF THE CONCLUSION, which is why the count is stated with its discriminator. Selecting heal commits by AUTHOR does not work in this repository: every session commits under the identity gunbc-ci-auto-heal, so that author matches 161 commits touching docs/design-failure-modes.md, of which most are ordinary session work. Heal is separated by its exact commit SUBJECT instead -- \"chore: regenerate drifted generated artifacts (ci auto-heal)\" -- which yields 54 on that path, against a negated-subject control of 253 that establishes the filter is not itself the answer. ",

    "THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT BOUNDS IT, which is what makes the row usable rather than a warning: it bites authority-only changes on carriers that HAVE a projection. A sibling lane's authority-only PR on gunbc.guarantee_stall drew zero heal commits, because no generated artifact consumes that carrier. Check whether the carrier has a projection before relying on the property. ",

    "NOT A WRITER-POPULATION PROBLEM, and this is the distinction that keeps it separate from a_deconfliction_plan_does_not_enumerate_its_writers: no other author is involved, none is omitted, and the author predicted nothing about anyone else. Heal does not COMPETE for the subject -- it derives an artifact from what the author already wrote. Counting it as a member of a writer set would widen that set to \"anything that can append a commit\", which includes the author's own CI, and the concept stops discriminating. What the two share is only the SYMPTOM that no conflict is produced so nothing notifies -- a symptom with at least three mechanisms, the third being the generated-artifact merge driver refusing with no markers. ",

    "RUNG: found BELOW the ladder. A public claim silently goes false and no typed refusal fires anywhere. ",

    "CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed, and REACHABLE WITHOUT NEW CAPABILITY -- which is the whole reason this is its own row. The predicate is single-ref and decidable today: whether the ref changed after the revision the claim was asserted against is answerable from that one ref's history, needing no cross-head enumeration, no open-head discovery and no declaration resolution. Filing it with the writer-population class would state one ceiling for both, park this affordable half behind that class's unbuilt capability, and reproduce exactly the grain mismatch section 4b(3) names as its own review tell. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the capability of binding a published branch claim to the revision it was asserted against, so the claim carries its own subject and a later derived push makes it re-adjudicable rather than merely stale. The affordable intermediate is a check that refuses when a claim about a path set is read at a ref whose head postdates the asserted revision. ",

    "REVIEW TELL: an author explaining that their change CANNOT collide because of which paths it touches. Ask whether the carrier has a generated projection, and whether the property is being asserted about the commit or about the branch a reader will actually fetch.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
